  "conclusions": [
    {
      "text": "The eleven exact IDs remain physical island/atoll records with their current parent IDs preserved. Governance and shipping groups have different scope from physical island identities.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "cook-marae-moana-island-roster",
        "cook-pa-enua-governance",
        "cook-shipping-policy-2026"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "No authoritative current island-scale boundary source with verified dataset vintage, complete named-land roster, license and retrievable bytes was available to establish coastline completeness. The eleven existing outlines remain unresolved, and this packet does not propose geometry or parent changes.",
      "status": "unresolved",
      "source_ids": [
        "cook-survey-boundary-custodian",
        "cook-linz-pacific-topo",
        "cookgeo-portal",
        "cookgov-lidar-launch-2026",
        "cookgeo-coverage-note",
        "natural-earth-admin1-2022"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The national roster names Nassau, Palmerston, Suwarrow and Takutea, with no Cook Islands-owned location feature in any baseline geography part file. Same-name Palmerston and Nassau features in Australia and the United States are foreign homonyms and not Cook Islands coverage; separate issue scope is needed to assess stable identities/parents and Takutea administrative versus physical semantics.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "cook-marae-moana-island-roster",
        "cook-pa-enua-governance",
        "cook-linz-pacific-topo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Atiu has a three-part generalized Natural Earth feature while the current physical Atiu record is one polygon. Takutea is separately identified 22 km northwest of Atiu. The comparison does not support adding Takutea to Atiu geometry or resolving the remaining component discrepancy.",
      "status": "unresolved",
      "source_ids": [
        "natural-earth-admin1-2022",
        "cook-takutea-assessment-2020",
        "cook-linz-pacific-topo"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Bounded follow-up: request CookGeo and Ministry of Justice dataset metadata, precise vintages, exact per-island component inventories and reuse terms; restore LINZ GeoTIFFs for licensed visual comparison; create a separate coverage task for the four named missing islands.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "cook-survey-boundary-custodian",
        "cook-linz-pacific-topo",
        "cookgeo-portal",
        "cookgov-lidar-launch-2026",
        "cookgeo-coverage-note"
      ]
    }
